  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Montana federal contract obligations are $948M for FY2026 to date. Award activity includes 6,260 actions with an average award size of $152K, and obligations fell 17.3% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buying agency with $324M, followed by the Department of Agriculture with $233M and the Department of Homeland Security with $170M. Contracting in FY2026 to date concentrates in a few industries: Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation leads with $144M, Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance follows with $137M, and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction accounts for $123M. Top vendors reflect those industry concentrations: S & K SECURITY GROUP LLC received $135M, ARCHER WESTERN FEDERAL JV received $58.8M, and PAF ELECTRICAL, INC. received $57M. Year-by-year obligations show growth through FY25 then a partial-year pullback: FY21 was $691M, FY22 was $925M, FY23 was $1B, FY24 was $1.1B, FY25 was $1.1B, and FY26 is $948M. These figures are contract obligations and the FY2026 total is a fiscal year to date figure.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did FY2026 obligations compare with recent years?",
        "body": "Montana obligations in FY26 are $948M, which follows a multi-year rise that peaked at $1.1B in FY24 and FY25. FY21 was $691M, FY22 was $925M, and FY23 was $1B. Obligations fell 17.3% year over year into the FY2026 to date total."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies, industries, and vendors dominate FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense leads buyers with $324M, followed by the Department of Agriculture with $233M and the Department of Homeland Security with $170M. Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation, Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance, and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction are the top industries at $144M, $137M, and $123M respectively. S & K SECURITY GROUP LLC, ARCHER WESTERN FEDERAL JV, and PAF ELECTRICAL, INC. are the top vendors at $135M, $58.8M, and $57M respectively."
      }
    ]
  },
